      "writtenOn": "2026-06-04T14:41:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Previously, the `conn` could have been `null`. Do we envisage a case where Jetty 12 could return a `null` here? Is it worth adding a precondition check just-in-case?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 63,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "dcb1e7bf94f42f73de30f7a0e86b52ef2d227466",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aca4c3e8_5a24c66a",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/pgm/http/jetty/HiddenErrorHandler.java",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 63,
      "author": {
        "id": 1011323
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-05T05:47:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The previous `conn \u003d\u003d null` check guarded `HttpConnection.getCurrentConnection()` — a ThreadLocal lookup that could legitimately return null. The new `baseRequest` is the parameter Jetty passes into `ErrorHandler.handle(target, baseRequest, req, res)`, and Jetty\u0027s contract guarantees its non-null for the duration of the call.\n\nA precondition check here would be guarding against a Jetty contract violation rather than a legitimate code path, so I\u0027d prefer not to add one — that way a real Jetty bug would surface as an NPE we can debug, rather than silently falling back to an empty error message. Happy to add a defensive `requireNonNull` if you still prefer the explicit crash for clarity.",
      "parentUuid": "12db88eb_279b76bf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 63,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "dcb1e7bf94f42f73de30f7a0e86b52ef2d227466",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
